## Examples
<Stories includePrimary={false} title="" />

## Usage

The IconLibrary component uses a name-based approach to reference SVG icons:

<Source
  language="tsx"
  dark
  code={`
import { IconLibrary } from '@lib/IconLibrary/IconLibrary';

// Basic usage
<IconLibrary name="star-line" />

// With custom size
<IconLibrary name="play-large-fill" className="w-6 h-6" />

// With custom color
<IconLibrary name="volume-up-fill" className="text-blue-500" />
`}
/>

### Styling Options

The IconLibrary component:

- Uses the `fill-current` utility to inherit color from text color
- Sets height to `1em` by default, making it scale with text size
- Supports all SVG attributes like `className`, `aria-label`, etc.

<Source
  language="tsx"
  dark
  code={`
import { IconLibrary } from '@lib/IconLibrary/IconLibrary';

function IconStylingExamples() {
  return (
    <div className="space-y-4">
      {/* Icons inherit text color */}
      <div className="text-red-500">
        <IconLibrary name="star-line" /> Text-colored icon
      </div>

      {/* Icons inherit text size */}
      <div className="text-2xl">
        <IconLibrary name="play-large-fill" /> Larger icon
      </div>

      {/* Custom classes override defaults */}
      <div>
        <IconLibrary
          name="volume-up-fill"
          className="h-8 w-8 text-blue-500"
        />
        Custom-sized and colored icon
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
`}
/>

## TypeScript Integration

The component provides types for all available icons:

<Source
  language="tsx"
  dark
  code={`
import { IconLibrary } from '@lib/IconLibrary/IconLibrary';
import { type IconName } from '@lib/IconLibrary/data';

// Type-safe icon names with autocompletion
const iconName: IconName = 'star-line';

function IconSelector({ selectedIcon, onSelect }) {
  return (
    <div className="flex gap-2">
      {['star-line', 'play-large-fill', 'volume-up-fill'].map((name) => (
        <button
          key={name}
          onClick={() => onSelect(name)}
          className={selectedIcon === name ? 'text-blue-500' : ''}
        >
          <IconLibrary name={name as IconName} className="h-6 w-6" />
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
`}
/>

## Bundle Size Considerations

Note that this component includes all icons in your bundle. For production applications where bundle size is critical, consider using the individual Icon components instead:

<Source
  language="tsx"
  dark
  code={`
// Recommended approach for production applications
import { Icon } from '@lib/Icon';
import { ReactComponent as StarLineSvg } from '@lib/assets/svgs/star-line.svg';
import { ReactComponent as PlayLargeFillSvg } from '@lib/assets/svgs/play-large-fill.svg';

function OptimizedIcons() {
  return (
    <div className="flex gap-4">
      <Icon as={StarLineSvg} className="text-yellow-400" />
      <Icon as={PlayLargeFillSvg} className="text-blue-500" />
    </div>
  );
}
`}
/>

The IconLibrary component is ideal for internal tools, documentation, or applications where developer convenience is prioritized over bundle size optimization. 